WEBVTT


00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.655
Hurry up!


00:00:34.284 --> 00:00:35.911
Come on, let's go!


00:01:12.823 --> 00:01:14.116
Go, go!


00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.399
No! No! No!


00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:23.769
- Call it off!
- I can't.


00:02:23.894 --> 00:02:26.772
It's doing what you want, so call it off!


00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:33.529
You didn't even stop the truck.


00:02:34.238 --> 00:02:36.865
My Angie lay dying in a ditch.


00:02:36.907 --> 00:02:39.409
I'm sorry about Angela. You know that.
We were...


00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:42.204
- Drunk?
- No, I was going to say we were wrong.


00:02:42.287 --> 00:02:44.623
We should've stopped.
We should've helped her.


00:02:44.748 --> 00:02:48.752
We should've gone to jail for what we done,
but killing us won't bring her back.


00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:13.610
- Call it off!
- For Angela.


00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:15.946
Well, I'm taking you with me.


00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.247
Please don't.


00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:38.844
All you got was a reprieve, Dallas.


00:03:39.928 --> 00:03:42.472
Yeah. One day he'll be coming back,


00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:45.976
and there'll be no place you can hide.


00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:48.937
There's a price to be paid for doing wrong,


00:03:49.521 --> 00:03:51.690
and there ain't no running from it.


00:03:51.815 --> 00:03:54.860
I'm cursed for life,
is that what you're saying?


00:03:54.985 --> 00:03:56.653
Longer than that.


00:03:57.279 --> 00:03:59.531
A whole lot longer than that.


00:06:58.836 --> 00:07:00.754
Something queer about that boy.


00:07:00.838 --> 00:07:03.507
My boy's just shy, that's all.


00:07:07.219 --> 00:07:08.387
Hey.


00:07:09.012 --> 00:07:11.640
- Do you wanna dance with me?
- No, thanks.


00:07:13.725 --> 00:07:15.686
Come on, I don't bite.


00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.897
It's just I'm promised to someone else,
that's all.


00:07:19.022 --> 00:07:20.858
Yeah, and who's that?


00:07:45.215 --> 00:07:46.884
Sorry we're late.


00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:49.803
We have a present for the bride.


00:07:50.721 --> 00:07:53.557
- You ain't coming in, boys.
- 'Cause we're Hatfields?


00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.684
We ain't allowed to celebrate
no McCoy wedding,


00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.978
is that what you're saying?


00:07:58.061 --> 00:08:02.316
You McCoys, always thinking
you're better than everyone else.


00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:03.442
Yeah.


00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:07.237
Not everyone else.


00:08:07.946 --> 00:08:09.615
Just you Hatfields.


00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:13.827
- Come on, now, Bobby Joe.
- Wait!


00:08:13.911 --> 00:08:15.829
Let's see what you got.


00:08:16.663 --> 00:08:19.625
Please, Bobby Joe, don't hurt them.


00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:22.252
Just 'cause they're idiots, they can't help it.


00:08:22.294 --> 00:08:25.130
'Cause you ask so nice, Jodie, okay.


00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:28.300
We know we can't go in.
They're just being dumb.


00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:30.636
- Hey, hey!
- And drunk.


00:08:30.761 --> 00:08:32.095
I'm sorry.


00:08:32.429 --> 00:08:35.724
I'm sorry, too, Jodie,
but no Hatfields are allowed.


00:08:35.807 --> 00:08:37.851
It's just the way it is.


00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:39.520
No offense.


00:08:39.603 --> 00:08:41.021
No offense?


00:08:41.188 --> 00:08:44.107
Stuck-up McCoys with your fancy weddings.


00:08:48.612 --> 00:08:49.988
You're lucky.


00:08:50.113 --> 00:08:51.281
Lucky.


00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.203
Go on home and sleep it off.


00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:00.332
What the hell are you doing?


00:09:00.457 --> 00:09:02.042
Let them have their wedding.


00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:05.295
No McCoy's going to have
a peaceful wedding


00:09:05.504 --> 00:09:08.549
as long as there is Hatfields around. Okay?


00:09:08.632 --> 00:09:10.467
What did we just do?


00:09:12.678 --> 00:09:15.138
- Yeah.
- Distracted the big man, that's all.


00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.474
Why? What for?


00:09:17.558 --> 00:09:20.102
You'll see. Oh, yeah, you'll see.


00:09:20.185 --> 00:09:22.229
Yeah, you'll see, Jodie.


00:09:43.333 --> 00:09:44.626
Sorry.


00:09:45.836 --> 00:09:47.838
Why don't you come and dance with Ricky?


00:09:47.921 --> 00:09:50.340
- No, he's weird.
- No.


00:09:50.382 --> 00:09:52.634
Ricky, come on,
why don't you dance a bit, huh?


00:09:52.718 --> 00:09:56.013
Just dance with her.
Daddy's getting suspicious.


00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.682
- How about you?
- Forget about it.


00:09:58.765 --> 00:10:02.978
Not your sister, dummy. A girl, like a date.
Just dance with her.


00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:04.771
I can't.


00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:07.649
Your beloved ain't gonna mind.


00:10:07.733 --> 00:10:09.026
She ain't even gonna know.


00:10:09.109 --> 00:10:10.611
But I'd know.


00:10:13.614 --> 00:10:16.783
It'll never work out. You know that, right?


00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:19.411
Only if we're dumb enough
to stay around here.


00:10:19.536 --> 00:10:24.833
This is home, Ricky. This is where we live.
This is what we know.


00:10:30.797 --> 00:10:33.926
You Hatfield sons of bitches. Get out!


00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:35.552
Get out!


00:10:41.141 --> 00:10:43.060
It's our special day.


00:10:44.311 --> 00:10:45.729
Calm down.


00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:47.523
Oh, come on, now.


00:10:52.569 --> 00:10:54.363
Come on, now.


00:10:55.656 --> 00:10:59.409
My cake! Not my cake. Not my cake!


00:11:04.122 --> 00:11:05.624
My cake.


00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.295
No, no, no, no! Stop it, y'all! Stop it!


00:11:20.556 --> 00:11:23.225
Oh, no. Oh, not the cake, no.


00:11:29.982 --> 00:11:31.942
Come on, get off him.


00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.033
Not the window!


00:11:41.493 --> 00:11:42.661
Boys!


00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:45.497
Y'all stop it.


00:11:47.082 --> 00:11:48.834
No!


00:12:04.349 --> 00:12:06.727
Oh, it's ruined.


00:12:14.985 --> 00:12:18.030
Oh, no!


00:12:35.547 --> 00:12:36.632
Yeah!


00:12:40.886 --> 00:12:44.932
That was great.
Did you see me stick one on his chin?


00:12:45.265 --> 00:12:48.185
What the hell did you go and do that for?


00:12:48.685 --> 00:12:51.104
We done it for you, Uncle Abner.


00:12:54.233 --> 00:12:55.984
To the Hatfields.


00:12:58.695 --> 00:13:00.739
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.


00:13:01.281 --> 00:13:03.450
Just the stupid feud again.


00:13:04.701 --> 00:13:07.329
They attacked a McCoy wedding.


00:13:12.376 --> 00:13:14.920
- Where's Daddy?
- Upstairs.


00:13:26.515 --> 00:13:29.434
Why, Daddy? Why did you let them do it?


00:13:29.518 --> 00:13:30.769
Let them?


00:13:31.311 --> 00:13:33.730
Hell, I didn't give no say-so.


00:13:34.189 --> 00:13:36.441
They heard about the wedding
and that was it.


00:13:36.525 --> 00:13:39.736
- But you could have stopped them.
- Yeah, I could have.


00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.948
But, Jodie, you just don't know
what them McCoys are like.


00:13:43.031 --> 00:13:45.158
So why don't you tell me?


00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:49.830
Ain't like I haven't tried,
but you just want to see the best in them.


00:13:50.038 --> 00:13:52.291
The McCoys ruined this town.


00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:56.420
They stole the best land
and turned it to sand.


00:13:57.296 --> 00:14:01.049
Without them, this would be a rich town.
Only good folk.


00:14:01.508 --> 00:14:03.677
But they ruined everything.


00:14:04.887 --> 00:14:08.432
But folks like us, we got pride.
We don't forget.


00:14:10.267 --> 00:14:13.854
You ever ask your Uncle Abner
why he's been stuck in that damn chair


00:14:13.937 --> 00:14:15.147
since he was nine?


00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:16.481
He wouldn't tell me.


00:14:16.565 --> 00:14:21.195
The McCoys were the first family
around these parts to get a motorcar.


00:14:22.404 --> 00:14:27.451
They drove it around
as if they owned the town, going hog-wild.


00:14:29.494 --> 00:14:32.414
Abner was playing in the road one day


00:14:33.248 --> 00:14:36.084
and they hit him with that damn car.


00:14:36.502 --> 00:14:38.670
They wrecked both his legs.


00:14:39.296 --> 00:14:40.339
Oh.


00:14:43.217 --> 00:14:46.887
McCoys were supposed to give us the car
to make amends.


00:14:47.888 --> 00:14:49.890
But they were too cheap.


00:14:49.973 --> 00:14:51.975
They never handed over.


00:14:52.226 --> 00:14:54.645
That's why this feud started.


00:16:01.253 --> 00:16:04.131
You going out to see that McCoy boy?


00:16:04.923 --> 00:16:07.968
Uncle Abner. I thought you were sleeping.


00:16:08.218 --> 00:16:10.637
Well, I ain't as dumb as folks think.


00:16:10.929 --> 00:16:13.682
Please don't tell. Please.


00:16:15.392 --> 00:16:17.144
You love this boy?


00:16:17.895 --> 00:16:18.979
Yes.


00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.481
So much.


00:16:21.732 --> 00:16:23.442
Well, all right, then.


00:16:28.822 --> 00:16:32.451
Daddy told me what happened
when you were a boy,


00:16:32.576 --> 00:16:34.203
with the motorcar.


00:16:34.286 --> 00:16:37.414
It all started with me, sorry to say.


00:16:38.081 --> 00:16:41.335
Don't even know
what happened to the damn car.


00:16:41.418 --> 00:16:42.920
Nobody does.


00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.590
All right. You go.


00:16:46.632 --> 00:16:48.884
You go and see your boy.


00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:51.678
Just be careful.


00:16:51.929 --> 00:16:53.305
Thank you.


00:17:02.606 --> 00:17:04.483
Where we going, Ricky?


00:17:04.775 --> 00:17:06.777
The old well's just here.


00:17:22.376 --> 00:17:24.795
Oh, I'm so glad you didn't get hurt.


00:17:36.014 --> 00:17:37.975
I can look out for you,


00:17:38.058 --> 00:17:41.645
but it's gonna have to be cut a bit short,
after what happened at the wedding.


00:17:41.728 --> 00:17:44.481
- I tried to stop them.
- Ain't your fault.


00:17:44.565 --> 00:17:47.860
It just means
it's even more dangerous tonight.


00:18:07.629 --> 00:18:10.841
Where did she go, old man?
We saw her creeping out.


00:18:10.924 --> 00:18:14.303
Just tell us, Uncle Abner,
and we'll let you go.


00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:19.224
Don't make us have to bust up your chair.


00:18:29.818 --> 00:18:32.571
I can't stand my dad's stares anymore.


00:18:33.363 --> 00:18:36.158
Waiting to marry me off to some cousin,


00:18:37.201 --> 00:18:39.828
when all we wanna do is be together.


00:18:40.412 --> 00:18:42.414
They'll never allow it.


00:18:42.706 --> 00:18:44.833
Your father or my father.


00:18:46.168 --> 00:18:51.423
Sometimes it seems like
they'd sooner see us dead.


00:19:03.685 --> 00:19:06.605
So we leave.


00:19:08.398 --> 00:19:11.443
Leave everything? Everyone?


00:19:12.152 --> 00:19:14.238
We can't go where they would find us.


00:19:14.321 --> 00:19:17.324
They would come after us,
try and drag us back.


00:19:17.407 --> 00:19:18.742
Or worse.


00:19:18.825 --> 00:19:22.788
- And where would we go?
- Anywhere they can't find us.


00:19:23.413 --> 00:19:25.832
But, Ricky, all we know is here.


00:19:26.458 --> 00:19:28.001
All I know is


00:19:30.462 --> 00:19:31.880
I love you.


00:19:44.768 --> 00:19:46.812
Hey, what we got here?


00:19:50.899 --> 00:19:53.151
Hey, girl, be quiet now.


00:19:57.614 --> 00:20:00.367
Hey, come on, Billy Bob. What you doing?
That's a McCoy.


00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.369
Still better than a hole in the wall, man.


00:20:02.452 --> 00:20:04.663
You're a bad one, Billy Bob.


00:20:07.165 --> 00:20:09.001
Grab her wrists, man.


00:20:17.301 --> 00:20:19.011
Did you hear something?


00:20:19.094 --> 00:20:21.054
Nothing to worry about. We're safe.


00:20:21.138 --> 00:20:23.515
We got Sara looking out for us.


00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:36.320
Come on, girl, you know you want it.


00:20:59.051 --> 00:21:01.887
- I guess we lost her.
- I guess we did.


00:21:04.014 --> 00:21:05.349
Let's go.


00:21:17.444 --> 00:21:19.363
You no-good, dirty slut.


00:21:19.446 --> 00:21:22.324
McCoy, ain't you got no self-respect?


00:21:23.325 --> 00:21:24.868
Leave her alone!


00:21:24.952 --> 00:21:27.454
You know
what Daddy's gonna do to you, huh?


00:21:27.538 --> 00:21:30.165
There's screwing and then there's
screwing around with a McCoy.


00:21:30.249 --> 00:21:32.000
- Come on, Jodie. Stop it.
- Let her go!


00:21:32.084 --> 00:21:34.545
Get off me. Get off me!


00:21:34.628 --> 00:21:36.296
That was mistake number two, boy.


00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.174
Mistake number one
was dealing with my sister.


00:21:39.258 --> 00:21:43.011
- Where's Sara?
- Run away, like you should've done.


00:21:51.645 --> 00:21:53.730
Ricky! Let him go!


00:21:54.189 --> 00:21:57.526
- No McCoy gets his hands on a Hatfield.
- No!


00:22:01.822 --> 00:22:02.865
No!


00:22:03.156 --> 00:22:06.076
- No! Ricky!
- Get inside.


00:22:06.493 --> 00:22:07.578
No.


00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:09.663
- No!
- Yeah.


00:22:09.746 --> 00:22:11.957
You want to kill him!


00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.960
We're just taking him for a ride, that's all.


00:22:15.252 --> 00:22:17.045
Here we go.


00:22:17.129 --> 00:22:18.589
- Ricky!
- No!


00:22:20.257 --> 00:22:21.341
No!


00:22:24.678 --> 00:22:26.305
No!


00:22:26.847 --> 00:22:28.891
No, no!


00:22:29.558 --> 00:22:30.893
Ricky!


00:22:35.772 --> 00:22:37.941
No! No!


00:22:40.444 --> 00:22:41.486
No!


00:22:50.621 --> 00:22:51.663
Sara.


00:22:52.414 --> 00:22:53.582
Sara.


00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:56.418
Sara! Sara!


00:22:58.045 --> 00:22:59.254
Sara!


00:23:00.464 --> 00:23:01.590
Sara!


00:23:02.341 --> 00:23:03.550
Sara!


00:23:04.176 --> 00:23:05.344
Sara.


00:24:27.885 --> 00:24:30.345
You're the witch of the woods.


00:24:30.679 --> 00:24:32.472
Folks call me that.


00:24:32.931 --> 00:24:36.101
I know what you can do, and I need...


00:24:37.644 --> 00:24:39.354
I need your help.


00:24:42.608 --> 00:24:46.153
The kind of help you can give him
ain't any help at all.


00:24:46.236 --> 00:24:48.322
Ed Harley.


00:24:49.406 --> 00:24:50.532
Been a while.


00:24:50.657 --> 00:24:54.203
Whatever this boy wants,
send him on his way.


00:24:54.286 --> 00:24:56.955
We both know what he wants, Ed Harley.


00:24:57.247 --> 00:24:59.166
Same thing you wanted.


00:24:59.416 --> 00:25:02.169
Yeah, and I'm still paying the price for it.


00:25:02.252 --> 00:25:03.879
Don't let him make this mistake.


00:25:04.004 --> 00:25:07.382
In the end, it ain't for me to decide.


00:25:08.884 --> 00:25:12.513
But I ain't felt a rage like this


00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:17.684
since the time you came to me
with your dead boy.


00:25:19.353 --> 00:25:21.271
You have to warn him.


00:25:21.563 --> 00:25:24.525
Like I tried to warn you.


00:25:25.734 --> 00:25:28.695
Let it stay there, in hell, where it belongs.


00:25:28.820 --> 00:25:32.741
I already told you, it ain't for me to decide.


00:25:35.994 --> 00:25:38.080
A McCoy! How could you?


00:25:38.205 --> 00:25:40.249
This stupid feud's
got nothing to do with me.


00:25:40.332 --> 00:25:42.501
You're a Hatfield.
Of course it's got to do with you.


00:25:42.584 --> 00:25:45.504
It's about some car
nobody even remembers.


00:25:45.587 --> 00:25:48.423
It's about being a member of this family.


00:25:48.507 --> 00:25:51.385
It's about the McCoys being scum
and ruining this town.


00:25:51.468 --> 00:25:53.387
Daddy, I love him.


00:25:58.016 --> 00:26:00.394
You never say that to me again.


00:26:02.020 --> 00:26:03.230
Never.


00:26:06.483 --> 00:26:09.570
- Tommy and Billy Bob nearly killed him.
- Well, maybe they should've done.


00:26:09.653 --> 00:26:11.113
You want blood on your hands?


00:26:11.238 --> 00:26:14.283
Better that than have McCoy hands
on my daughter!


00:26:14.366 --> 00:26:16.952
- And his hands was all over her.
- Shut up!


00:26:25.377 --> 00:26:27.462
You go back to your room.


00:26:28.714 --> 00:26:31.675
You ain't never gonna see that boy again,
do you hear me?


00:26:32.384 --> 00:26:33.594
Never.


00:27:25.103 --> 00:27:27.481
You could've left him out there in the woods
where he'd be safe.


00:27:27.564 --> 00:27:30.317
Oh, and he would've come back here again.


00:27:30.651 --> 00:27:31.985
I told you.


00:27:32.069 --> 00:27:34.446
I seen a rage like this before.


00:27:35.197 --> 00:27:37.115
It don't drift away.


00:27:37.449 --> 00:27:39.284
Please, Haggis, just think on it.


00:27:39.368 --> 00:27:41.453
Ain't my place to do that.


00:27:41.620 --> 00:27:42.829
If he asks...


00:27:42.913 --> 00:27:45.791
Please, just tell him no
and send that boy home.


00:27:45.874 --> 00:27:46.875
We'll see.


00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.503
You're just a gatekeeper, ain't you?


00:27:49.628 --> 00:27:51.547
You're gonna be ash.


00:27:51.630 --> 00:27:55.551
- In a sack, screaming...
- We all got our curses, Ed Harley.


00:27:57.594 --> 00:27:59.721
Now go away, Ed Harley.


00:28:01.014 --> 00:28:02.724
I got work to do.


00:28:03.308 --> 00:28:05.143
Who you talking to?


00:28:05.227 --> 00:28:06.478
Nobody.


00:28:07.771 --> 00:28:10.357
Nobody when he was alive,


00:28:11.441 --> 00:28:13.360
and he's nobody now.


00:28:14.611 --> 00:28:16.071
Where's Sara?


00:28:16.280 --> 00:28:17.656
Outside.


00:28:18.699 --> 00:28:21.577
Been enough dead things in here already.


00:28:22.494 --> 00:28:23.704
Drink.


00:28:25.122 --> 00:28:27.040
They killed my sister.


00:28:27.499 --> 00:28:29.251
My little sister.


00:28:30.294 --> 00:28:32.045
The Hatfields did it.


00:28:32.379 --> 00:28:35.424
They killed her, then they tried to kill me


00:28:36.258 --> 00:28:38.218
because I love Jodie.


00:28:38.802 --> 00:28:43.432
They'll pay for this. I'll get them.
All of them. Every one of them.


00:28:43.557 --> 00:28:46.059
They won't get away with this.
I'll make them pay.


00:28:46.185 --> 00:28:50.022
What you're asking for has a name.


00:28:50.105 --> 00:28:51.523
Pumpkinhead.


00:28:51.607 --> 00:28:53.233
Vengeance.


00:28:56.528 --> 00:28:59.615
They killed my sister
because of the love I have for Jodie,


00:28:59.698 --> 00:29:01.950
and they gotta pay for that.


00:29:02.409 --> 00:29:04.745
I can't help loving her.


00:29:04.828 --> 00:29:08.749
Even tried to call it off for her sake.


00:29:10.292 --> 00:29:15.714
If a day goes by and I ain't seen her,
ain't held her, ain't kissed her,


00:29:15.797 --> 00:29:18.300
then it's like the day never came.


00:29:18.592 --> 00:29:21.720
I need her. She's everything to me.


00:29:21.803 --> 00:29:24.932
And her damn family
won't let us be together.


00:29:25.933 --> 00:29:30.437
Now they've killed Sara
and everything's different.


00:29:30.938 --> 00:29:32.731
If this is done,


00:29:33.440 --> 00:29:35.359
it can't be undone.


00:29:36.818 --> 00:29:39.905
The demon will do your bidding
till it's done.


00:29:40.989 --> 00:29:43.158
And then you pay the price.


00:29:44.034 --> 00:29:45.911
I don't care about the cost.


00:29:45.994 --> 00:29:51.041
If you do this, the Hatfields will pay
a terrible price for what they done.


00:29:51.917 --> 00:29:54.795
None of them will live to see the end of it.


00:29:54.878 --> 00:29:56.213
But you...


00:29:57.297 --> 00:29:59.883
You'll pay the worst price of all.


00:30:00.592 --> 00:30:02.135
What price?


00:30:02.261 --> 00:30:06.723
It's gonna cost you your very soul, boy.


00:30:07.975 --> 00:30:10.310
Your very soul.


00:30:10.894 --> 00:30:12.646
I can't walk away.


00:30:13.856 --> 00:30:17.192
I can't let them get away
with what they've done,


00:30:17.276 --> 00:30:19.528
and I need to be with Jodie.


00:30:20.070 --> 00:30:21.905
And this is the only way.


00:30:22.114 --> 00:30:24.074
Please, you gotta help me.


00:30:24.157 --> 00:30:26.493
You can't let them Hatfields
get away with this,


00:30:26.577 --> 00:30:29.830
and you can't let them
keep me and Jodie apart.


00:30:40.841 --> 00:30:42.593
Raise your hand.


00:30:46.638 --> 00:30:48.348
What do you want?


00:30:48.557 --> 00:30:49.641
Jodie.


00:30:49.725 --> 00:30:51.894
And the rest of the Hatfields?


00:30:52.978 --> 00:30:55.439
Dead, gone,


00:30:55.814 --> 00:31:01.361
for what they done to Sara, who never
hurt nobody her whole beautiful life.


00:31:03.822 --> 00:31:07.618
Your revenge will eat at your soul, boy,


00:31:08.452 --> 00:31:10.078
bit by bit.


00:31:11.121 --> 00:31:13.207
It ain't easy.


00:31:13.332 --> 00:31:15.459
But I'll still love Jodie?


00:31:18.837 --> 00:31:20.672
That's all I need.


00:31:39.399 --> 00:31:41.985
Mom! Dad!


00:31:42.903 --> 00:31:45.405
Mama! Daddy!


00:31:54.122 --> 00:31:56.416
- Sara!
- Sara.


00:31:57.084 --> 00:31:59.378
- Sara.
- Sara!


00:32:02.965 --> 00:32:04.424
Sara!


00:33:37.601 --> 00:33:40.896
- Who's there?
- Relax, just here for a drink.


00:33:42.606 --> 00:33:45.692
Did you hear something weird just then?
Like an animal.


00:33:45.776 --> 00:33:47.569
But no damn animal
I've ever heard around here.


00:33:47.694 --> 00:33:51.031
- I didn't hear nothing.
- Too drunk, probably.


00:33:52.157 --> 00:33:54.493
Best moonshine in the county.


00:33:55.869 --> 00:33:58.539
Yeah, that's the way I like it.


00:34:02.417 --> 00:34:03.418
Bear?


00:34:03.544 --> 00:34:04.878
Or worse.


00:34:07.172 --> 00:34:10.092
Nothing worse than a bear out there.


00:34:56.513 --> 00:34:57.890
Don't.


00:36:10.087 --> 00:36:11.797
I had a son once,


00:36:13.590 --> 00:36:16.468
and it's the only heaven I'll ever know.


00:36:18.011 --> 00:36:20.514
He slipped right through my fingers.


00:36:22.850 --> 00:36:25.352
No amount of love could save him.


00:36:26.103 --> 00:36:27.813
Life is so short.


00:36:31.733 --> 00:36:33.986
From one breath to the next.


00:36:35.028 --> 00:36:36.488
Who are you?


00:36:36.822 --> 00:36:38.198
Ed Harley.


00:36:38.407 --> 00:36:40.409
How did you get in here?


00:36:41.702 --> 00:36:44.079
Something terrible is happening,


00:36:45.414 --> 00:36:47.499
and only you can stop it.


00:36:47.958 --> 00:36:49.710
What are you talking about?


00:36:49.793 --> 00:36:52.171
Something's been set in motion,


00:36:52.629 --> 00:36:54.715
and only you can stop it.


00:36:55.674 --> 00:36:57.009
Only you.


00:37:06.685 --> 00:37:08.437
We are what we do.


00:37:51.730 --> 00:37:54.149
Dolly, why don't you
go get us some lemonade?


00:37:54.274 --> 00:37:56.151
Why don't you get it?


00:37:56.360 --> 00:37:59.655
'Cause I don't want to see Daddy,
that's why.


00:38:10.666 --> 00:38:11.667
Oh, my...


00:38:17.548 --> 00:38:20.175
I thought I never would see you again.


00:38:20.259 --> 00:38:22.344
They can't keep us apart.


00:38:24.638 --> 00:38:26.515
I love you. I'll always love you,


00:38:26.598 --> 00:38:29.685
no matter what anybody says
or anybody does.


00:38:29.810 --> 00:38:33.105
I thought my idiot brothers
were gonna kill you.


00:38:33.230 --> 00:38:35.190
They can't hurt me now.


00:38:35.691 --> 00:38:37.359
If they find you here, Ricky...


00:38:37.442 --> 00:38:41.029
I've done something
so that we can be together.


00:38:41.363 --> 00:38:43.448
Something's been set in motion.


00:38:43.532 --> 00:38:47.828
We will be together.
Soon they won't be able to keep us apart.


00:38:47.911 --> 00:38:50.956
Ricky, what have you done?


00:38:51.915 --> 00:38:53.125
Jodie?


00:38:53.792 --> 00:38:55.335
Where are you?


00:38:56.128 --> 00:38:57.337
Don't go.


00:38:57.421 --> 00:38:59.506
Tell me what you've done.


00:39:05.721 --> 00:39:07.139
I love you.


00:39:32.414 --> 00:39:36.835
- All right, lead the way.
- It was Jasper who found him.


00:39:37.503 --> 00:39:41.340
All torn up, he is,
like a wild animal got to him.


00:39:43.008 --> 00:39:45.427
Must've been one hell of a bear.


00:39:49.890 --> 00:39:52.267
Have you ever seen this before?


00:39:56.396 --> 00:39:57.439
No.


00:39:57.856 --> 00:39:59.358
That's a lie.


00:40:02.486 --> 00:40:04.696
You seen this before, ain't you?


00:40:04.780 --> 00:40:08.450
- You just stay away from me.
- You don't have to be afraid of me, Dallas.


00:40:08.575 --> 00:40:10.536
I ain't gonna hurt you.


00:40:10.619 --> 00:40:12.955
I'm just here to tell you the truth.


00:40:13.038 --> 00:40:15.082
- Truth?
- Yeah.


00:40:16.542 --> 00:40:20.003
- This isn't even real.
- I told you five years ago, didn't I?


00:40:20.420 --> 00:40:22.297
That this thing would be coming back.


00:40:22.381 --> 00:40:24.216
You've run out of time.


00:40:24.925 --> 00:40:28.595
Well, there's gotta be something I can do,


00:40:29.054 --> 00:40:30.389
somewhere I can go.


00:40:30.472 --> 00:40:32.766
You can go straight to hell.


00:40:46.905 --> 00:40:50.409
Keep away from Pumpkinhead,
unless you're tired of living.


00:40:50.492 --> 00:40:54.454
His enemies are mostly dead.
He's mean and unforgiving.


00:40:54.746 --> 00:40:55.956
Hey!


00:40:56.540 --> 00:40:57.666
Stop that.


00:40:57.708 --> 00:40:59.877
We were just telling her
about Pumpkinhead.


00:41:00.002 --> 00:41:01.879
Ain't no such thing.


00:41:02.212 --> 00:41:03.630
It's just a story,


00:41:03.714 --> 00:41:08.135
something nasty boys
tell nice little girls to scare them.


00:41:08.218 --> 00:41:11.180
It ain't real. Now go home.


00:41:13.640 --> 00:41:15.726
We was just funning with her.


00:41:15.851 --> 00:41:19.021
Didn't look like
she was having so much fun.


00:41:20.063 --> 00:41:21.690
You're wrong, though.


00:41:21.815 --> 00:41:25.986
Pumpkinhead's real. My daddy said so.
Said he's come from hell.


00:41:26.069 --> 00:41:27.654
Just a story.


00:41:27.738 --> 00:41:30.824
Folks around here
got too much time on their hands.


00:41:30.908 --> 00:41:35.204
Sorry to be the one to tell you,
but there ain't no Pumpkinhead.


00:41:35.829 --> 00:41:37.873
Tell that to Ed Harley.


00:41:38.498 --> 00:41:39.875
Did you say Ed Harley?


00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:41.919
Yeah, he was the one who first called him.


00:41:42.044 --> 00:41:43.587
Went up into the woods
and found the witch.


00:41:43.712 --> 00:41:44.880
The witch?


00:41:45.005 --> 00:41:48.383
Yeah, she lives up there,
about five miles west of here.


00:41:48.425 --> 00:41:51.553
- What happened to Ed Harley?
- He killed himself,


00:41:51.678 --> 00:41:55.682
but not before Pumpkinhead killed
all those who wronged him.


00:42:03.190 --> 00:42:05.943
She was such a sweet girl.


00:42:18.539 --> 00:42:22.292
They found another Hatfield,
all burned up by that old still.


00:42:23.877 --> 00:42:25.754
They did that for Sara?


00:42:26.296 --> 00:42:28.298
Then they had it coming.


00:42:48.819 --> 00:42:52.447
If it was a bear, this'll take care of him.


00:42:52.906 --> 00:42:54.575
It killed Tommy.


00:42:56.827 --> 00:42:58.662
Okay, trap's all set.


00:42:59.413 --> 00:43:00.956
We hear him get caught,


00:43:01.081 --> 00:43:05.919
then come and watch that bear
trying to chew his own leg off to get away.


00:43:06.003 --> 00:43:07.171
I seen it once.


00:43:07.296 --> 00:43:11.258
Sat and watched it for maybe an hour.


00:43:14.178 --> 00:43:16.471
Tommy was with me that night.


00:43:17.181 --> 00:43:18.682
Okay, let's go.


00:43:26.023 --> 00:43:28.150
There was nothing
that we could do about it.


00:43:28.275 --> 00:43:32.154
He ain't got over the shock of finding her.


00:43:48.045 --> 00:43:49.963
What's up, Charlie?


00:44:02.142 --> 00:44:03.977
Ain't nothing there.


00:44:05.020 --> 00:44:06.855
Charlie, you faggot.


00:44:30.754 --> 00:44:32.005
Charlie!


00:44:33.507 --> 00:44:34.508
Charlie!


00:45:15.799 --> 00:45:18.260
- No, don't go. Don't leave me.
- Hold on.


00:45:23.265 --> 00:45:25.100
I can't open it.


00:45:27.728 --> 00:45:31.982
- I'm gonna have to cut you free.
- Are you crazy? Cut off my damn leg?


00:45:35.736 --> 00:45:38.155
Come on, do it. Do it.


00:45:39.990 --> 00:45:41.074
Do it!


00:45:52.961 --> 00:45:54.630
Sorry, Billy Bob.


00:46:57.901 --> 00:46:59.862
Ricky, what's wrong?


00:46:59.987 --> 00:47:01.196
Ricky.


00:47:05.576 --> 00:47:07.160
Leave me alone!


00:47:09.663 --> 00:47:11.832
What's wrong with you, man?


00:47:17.754 --> 00:47:20.215
Ricky, don't leave.


00:47:22.217 --> 00:47:23.760
Leave me alone.


00:47:40.110 --> 00:47:41.695
Dale, wait.


00:48:34.998 --> 00:48:36.458
What the...


00:48:44.007 --> 00:48:46.260
Hey. Hey. Hey, boy.


00:48:46.426 --> 00:48:49.304
Pumpkinhead. He's real.


00:48:49.346 --> 00:48:50.806
I seen him.


00:48:52.099 --> 00:48:53.976
He killed my brothers.


00:48:55.686 --> 00:48:57.104
He's real.


00:48:57.187 --> 00:49:00.357
I saw. It was Pumpkinhead.


00:50:45.879 --> 00:50:47.089
Hello?


00:50:50.425 --> 00:50:52.469
My name's Jodie Hatfield.


00:50:53.762 --> 00:50:58.725
I'm here to talk to you about Ricky McCoy
and Ed Harley.


00:52:25.562 --> 00:52:28.148
That boy must really love you,


00:52:28.232 --> 00:52:30.692
you being a Hatfield and all.


00:52:30.734 --> 00:52:33.153
He ain't gonna kill you.


00:52:33.403 --> 00:52:37.491
Like I said, the boy really loves you.


00:53:00.764 --> 00:53:03.225
Y'all look like you got bad news.


00:53:05.394 --> 00:53:09.356
The four that went out last night
ain't coming back, right?


00:53:13.235 --> 00:53:15.612
So was it a bear that got them?


00:53:18.198 --> 00:53:19.867
Weren't no bear.


00:53:23.412 --> 00:53:25.914
Then it must've been the McCoys.


00:54:03.493 --> 00:54:07.748
He wants your whole clan dead
so you can be together,


00:54:07.956 --> 00:54:10.459
and for what they done to his sister.


00:54:10.584 --> 00:54:13.462
Poor Sara.
She never should have got involved.


00:54:13.504 --> 00:54:16.089
Your idiot brothers
should never have killed her.


00:54:16.173 --> 00:54:17.966
You don't know that.


00:54:18.175 --> 00:54:21.637
Maybe she just fell.
We don't know they did anything.


00:54:21.762 --> 00:54:24.264
Ain't gonna get to ask them now.


00:54:25.766 --> 00:54:27.100
They're both dead?


00:54:27.184 --> 00:54:29.478
And they ain't the only ones.


00:54:31.021 --> 00:54:33.607
And you called that thing for him?


00:54:34.358 --> 00:54:40.447
You let Ricky sentence my family to death
for something they maybe didn't even do?


00:54:40.531 --> 00:54:42.324
It ain't her fault.


00:54:42.866 --> 00:54:45.994
She tried to tell him what the cost would be.


00:54:46.703 --> 00:54:49.373
But in the end, it ain't her decision.


00:54:49.498 --> 00:54:51.458
Ed Harley.


00:54:52.668 --> 00:54:54.002
Back again.


00:54:54.044 --> 00:54:56.839
Yeah, that's my curse,
and there ain't no end to it.


00:54:56.880 --> 00:54:59.174
- You have to call it off.
- Can't.


00:54:59.383 --> 00:55:02.135
He stays till the killing is done,
then he goes back.


00:55:02.177 --> 00:55:03.679
That's just the way of it.


00:55:03.804 --> 00:55:04.972
Ricky, then.


00:55:05.055 --> 00:55:07.349
Ricky brought it here. He can call it off.


00:55:07.474 --> 00:55:10.310
You're the only one that can stop it, Jodie.


00:55:10.394 --> 00:55:11.520
How?


00:55:12.896 --> 00:55:15.023
Do you remember what I told you?


00:55:15.148 --> 00:55:16.859
We are what we do.


00:55:17.651 --> 00:55:19.403
You're gonna have to do
the hardest thing there is.


00:55:19.528 --> 00:55:21.154
What does that mean?


00:55:21.196 --> 00:55:23.907
You'll know when the time comes.


00:55:25.993 --> 00:55:29.079
Tell me. What does he mean?


00:55:29.204 --> 00:55:32.666
Means what he says. That's all.


00:55:41.758 --> 00:55:44.553
Sorry to be the one to tell you this, Jim.


00:55:44.636 --> 00:55:47.055
It's the worst part of the job.


00:55:49.725 --> 00:55:52.769
I don't see how a bear
could've got all of them.


00:55:53.061 --> 00:55:56.648
They was experienced hunters.
I taught them myself.


00:55:58.609 --> 00:56:00.986
It ain't no bear doing this.


00:56:01.820 --> 00:56:05.490
Bears just don't go after one family,
and we got six dead men now.


00:56:05.616 --> 00:56:07.326
They all got the Hatfield name.


00:56:07.451 --> 00:56:09.453
Are you saying the McCoys are doing this


00:56:09.578 --> 00:56:12.915
and taking some kind of revenge
for what happened to that little girl?


00:56:12.956 --> 00:56:15.626
- Not the McCoys.
- Well, then who?


00:56:16.752 --> 00:56:20.714
It's not who, Jim. It's what.
You've heard of Pumpkinhead?


00:56:20.797 --> 00:56:24.927
That's just a legend,
one of them campfire tales.


00:56:25.344 --> 00:56:26.762
It's real.


00:56:27.137 --> 00:56:28.972
Ed Harley started it.


00:56:29.139 --> 00:56:33.101
Ed Harley went crazy, killed some kids,
then shot himself.


00:56:33.310 --> 00:56:35.687
Everything else were just made-up lies.


00:56:35.812 --> 00:56:37.689
He called Pumpkinhead.


00:56:38.315 --> 00:56:42.444
Ed Harley never killed no city kids.
The only man Ed ever hurt were himself.


00:56:42.486 --> 00:56:45.781
Now, Pumpkinhead's back,
and it's killing your family.


00:56:45.822 --> 00:56:50.786
It's got six so far, and if we don't fight back,
it's going to get the rest of you.


00:56:50.827 --> 00:56:53.163
You're crazy. You been in the sun too long.


00:56:53.288 --> 00:56:55.207
I got six deaths to grieve,


00:56:55.290 --> 00:56:59.628
and you come up here with
these old wives' tales and scary stories.


00:56:59.962 --> 00:57:01.505
It's real, Jim.


00:57:02.130 --> 00:57:05.801
You just gotta ask Jimmy Langford.
It's what Dale told him before he died.


00:57:05.843 --> 00:57:07.219
Pumpkinhead attacked him.


00:57:07.302 --> 00:57:10.681
Jimmy Langford is a damn drunk
and you're supposed to be the damn sheriff.


00:57:10.806 --> 00:57:14.309
- I got no time for this!
- He's telling the truth, Daddy.


00:57:14.476 --> 00:57:15.811
I seen it.


00:57:17.145 --> 00:57:19.314
It was Ricky who called it.


00:57:19.648 --> 00:57:22.484
That McCoy boy you've been messing with?


00:57:22.693 --> 00:57:26.989
He blamed Billy Bob and Tommy
for what happened to his sister, Sara,


00:57:27.865 --> 00:57:30.409
and he called the demon to kill...


00:57:31.827 --> 00:57:34.538
- To kill us all.
- I seen it, Daddy.


00:57:35.414 --> 00:57:37.666
It was right in front of me.


00:57:38.500 --> 00:57:40.002
And I'm sorry,


00:57:41.587 --> 00:57:45.257
but I'm the only one Ricky won't let it kill.


00:57:46.550 --> 00:57:47.926
I'm sorry.


00:57:50.762 --> 00:57:52.931
Come on, it's payback time.


00:58:20.918 --> 00:58:22.503
Brett, what are you doing?


00:58:22.586 --> 00:58:25.047
- Getting some payback on the McCoys.
- The McCoys didn't...


00:58:25.130 --> 00:58:28.425
Hold up there, now. Whatever you boys
think you're doing, you got it wrong.


00:58:28.550 --> 00:58:31.595
We're gonna do what we should've done
years ago, burn them out.


00:58:33.639 --> 00:58:36.558
Now, y'all listen to me. You got it wrong.


00:58:36.600 --> 00:58:39.728
It's not the McCoys that are killing
your brothers and your cousins.


00:58:39.811 --> 00:58:41.480
It's Pumpkinhead.


00:58:41.563 --> 00:58:45.067
- Ain't no such thing, Sheriff.
- No, it's real and it's back.


00:58:45.150 --> 00:58:47.569
It's just a story.
You're just trying to protect the McCoys.


00:58:47.653 --> 00:58:49.571
- Yeah.
- He's telling the truth, Brett!


00:58:49.655 --> 00:58:52.074
Only one kind of monster
living around these parts,


00:58:52.157 --> 00:58:53.951
and they all got the name McCoy.


00:58:54.076 --> 00:58:55.661
We're gonna burn them out once and for all.


00:58:55.786 --> 00:58:58.830
Now, I can't let you boys do that.


00:59:02.292 --> 00:59:04.294
No. Don't do this.


00:59:04.795 --> 00:59:06.588
Don't. Here, guys.


00:59:06.672 --> 00:59:08.507
Guys, just listen!


00:59:08.590 --> 00:59:09.967
Listen!


00:59:10.425 --> 00:59:12.761
Why are you doing this, Brett?


00:59:12.803 --> 00:59:14.096
- Leave us.
- Don't!


00:59:14.179 --> 00:59:16.723
You're only going to make things worse.


00:59:16.849 --> 00:59:18.392
Damn you!


00:59:20.769 --> 00:59:21.937
Right.


00:59:39.663 --> 00:59:42.499
- He's still our son.
- I don't know where he is.


00:59:42.624 --> 00:59:45.586
You saw. He went off into the woods,
told us to leave him alone.


00:59:45.669 --> 00:59:49.381
He was upset. What if the Hatfields
get into their dumb heads


00:59:49.464 --> 00:59:52.968
that he's the one doing all that killing,
killing all their brothers?


00:59:53.051 --> 00:59:55.512
- Boy gotta look after himself.
- He's not like the others.


00:59:55.637 --> 00:59:58.724
He's sensitive.
He's not tough like the others.


00:59:58.849 --> 01:00:01.351
You can't just leave him all alone
in the woods.


01:00:01.476 --> 01:00:03.061
Dad, open up.


01:00:04.354 --> 01:00:07.399
- Bunch of Hatfields have pulled up.
- Oh, no.


01:00:09.026 --> 01:00:10.569
Damn! What now?


01:00:31.048 --> 01:00:32.257
Do it.


01:00:37.679 --> 01:00:39.181
Go on.


01:00:49.858 --> 01:00:51.026
Wait!


01:00:52.277 --> 01:00:54.613
What are you doing? Brett!


01:00:54.863 --> 01:00:56.698
Get out of here!


01:00:58.784 --> 01:01:00.536
Come on, boys.


01:01:00.744 --> 01:01:02.579
You're going to pay for this.


01:01:03.038 --> 01:01:05.415
Stop! Stop!


01:01:05.541 --> 01:01:07.000
Stop it!


01:01:08.085 --> 01:01:10.128
Stop it! Stop it!


01:01:17.636 --> 01:01:19.471
Help!


01:01:19.721 --> 01:01:20.848
Listen.


01:01:20.931 --> 01:01:22.307
- Help!
- Listen.


01:01:22.432 --> 01:01:25.936
Listen! Stop it! Stop it. Listen.


01:01:26.103 --> 01:01:27.145
Stop it.


01:01:27.271 --> 01:01:28.564
- Help me!
- Listen.


01:01:28.647 --> 01:01:30.732
- Stop! Everybody, stop it!
- Help!


01:01:30.983 --> 01:01:33.235
I'm burning in here!


01:01:33.443 --> 01:01:34.736
Mama?


01:01:35.279 --> 01:01:36.738
Help me!


01:01:37.406 --> 01:01:39.575
Boys, help me!


01:01:40.742 --> 01:01:43.245
Somebody help me!


01:01:51.503 --> 01:01:54.923
Ricky! Somebody!


01:01:55.966 --> 01:01:57.676
Help me!


01:01:58.969 --> 01:02:01.930
Get out of the way. Get out of the way!


01:02:11.690 --> 01:02:12.983
Help!


01:02:17.946 --> 01:02:20.782
Somebody help me!


01:02:22.784 --> 01:02:23.827
Help!


01:02:32.503 --> 01:02:33.795
Help!


01:02:37.799 --> 01:02:39.384
Help me!


01:02:40.969 --> 01:02:42.888
I'm dying!


01:02:45.307 --> 01:02:47.267
Somebody help!


01:02:54.983 --> 01:02:56.235
Come on.


01:02:56.985 --> 01:03:00.072
- Come on. Come on, here.
- Jodie! Jodie, help me.


01:03:00.572 --> 01:03:03.617
- Here, put this over your head.
- Please get me down.


01:03:13.669 --> 01:03:15.087
Oh, my God!


01:03:16.046 --> 01:03:17.840
Quick, Jodie.


01:03:20.592 --> 01:03:21.885
I can't.


01:03:24.680 --> 01:03:25.848
I can't.


01:03:25.931 --> 01:03:28.183
Then we're both gonna die.


01:03:33.689 --> 01:03:35.190
Grab hold.


01:03:53.584 --> 01:03:56.211
Get back up there. Jodie's still up there.


01:04:00.465 --> 01:04:02.384
- Come on, Jodie!
- Jodie!


01:04:03.051 --> 01:04:04.094
Run and jump.


01:04:04.720 --> 01:04:06.638
Jump, Jodie.


01:04:11.226 --> 01:04:12.895
Now jump.


01:04:15.981 --> 01:04:18.150
It's all right, let her down.


01:04:18.400 --> 01:04:21.069
Give me your hand. Come on. It's okay.


01:04:21.111 --> 01:04:24.281
It's all right. It's all right.


01:04:48.263 --> 01:04:50.390
I never seen Daddy so mad.


01:04:50.516 --> 01:04:53.018
He said even McCoys don't deserve
what they did.


01:04:53.101 --> 01:04:56.104
He's right. It's not their fault.


01:04:56.313 --> 01:04:58.774
It's not them who are doing this.


01:04:58.815 --> 01:05:00.275
It's Ricky.


01:05:00.817 --> 01:05:02.986
Ricky McCoy? The boy you...


01:05:03.111 --> 01:05:07.032
The whole thing's more my fault
than the rest of the McCoys.


01:05:07.991 --> 01:05:12.287
He did what he did 'cause he wanted us
to be free to be together.


01:05:12.788 --> 01:05:14.873
And now six men are dead


01:05:15.791 --> 01:05:18.627
and the McCoys lost their house
and a lot more than that,


01:05:18.669 --> 01:05:20.379
and all 'cause of me.


01:05:20.504 --> 01:05:22.214
What did Ricky do?


01:05:23.340 --> 01:05:25.884
What did Ricky do that was so bad?


01:05:26.134 --> 01:05:30.681
Called something
that he should've left alone.


01:05:33.976 --> 01:05:35.978
Gonna kill an old woman?


01:05:37.062 --> 01:05:39.481
Gonna do it in Billy Bob's name?


01:05:40.649 --> 01:05:42.317
How about Tommy?


01:05:42.693 --> 01:05:44.695
You think he'd be proud?


01:05:57.708 --> 01:05:59.334
Well, I'll be.


01:06:14.892 --> 01:06:17.227
I ain't here for more trouble.


01:06:18.228 --> 01:06:20.606
There's been death on both sides.


01:06:22.733 --> 01:06:26.111
We lost our little Sara, our house.


01:06:28.447 --> 01:06:30.365
I know you lost more.


01:06:31.200 --> 01:06:32.868
Six of our boys.


01:06:33.035 --> 01:06:37.497
We don't put a stop to this,
we're all gonna end up in the ground.


01:06:37.873 --> 01:06:40.918
Now, this here's the car
that knocked down Abner.


01:06:42.794 --> 01:06:44.379
Now it's yours.


01:06:46.048 --> 01:06:47.883
I'm calling a truce,


01:06:48.592 --> 01:06:50.385
for all our sakes.


01:07:03.815 --> 01:07:07.444
So now it's over?


01:07:08.570 --> 01:07:10.447
Wish it was that easy.


01:07:11.406 --> 01:07:12.741
What do you mean?


01:07:12.783 --> 01:07:15.077
Your boy Ricky.
You don't know what he done?


01:07:15.160 --> 01:07:16.912
Been acting real strange.


01:07:16.995 --> 01:07:19.122
We got a powerful problem.


01:07:19.915 --> 01:07:21.917
We gonna need your help.


01:07:30.843 --> 01:07:35.973
We are not gonna listen to you! No way.
It ain't gonna happen. Not anymore.


01:07:37.182 --> 01:07:39.434
Sit down, Hatfield, and control your boys.


01:07:39.518 --> 01:07:40.811
It ain't gonna happen.


01:07:48.277 --> 01:07:51.446
Tell me something.
Why don't you shut up over there, all right?


01:07:55.784 --> 01:07:57.786
Sit down, Hatfield. Just come here.


01:08:02.457 --> 01:08:04.209
Tell them, Papa.


01:08:06.962 --> 01:08:09.715
Hatfield, control those boys.
Get them to sit down.


01:08:09.840 --> 01:08:11.133
Sit down!


01:08:12.384 --> 01:08:14.136
Shut up!


01:08:16.471 --> 01:08:19.141
What Ricky done
had nothing to do with the rest of us.


01:08:19.183 --> 01:08:20.726
We ain't saying it has,


01:08:20.851 --> 01:08:24.229
- but we have to stop this thing.
- But six of us are dead because of him.


01:08:24.313 --> 01:08:25.939
- Yeah!
- Sit down.


01:08:26.148 --> 01:08:27.816
Six of us are dead.


01:08:30.152 --> 01:08:32.863
Come on, shut up. Shut up!


01:08:33.405 --> 01:08:34.865
You ought to be in bed.


01:08:34.990 --> 01:08:36.825
What are they gonna do?


01:08:36.909 --> 01:08:40.704
I don't know. Come on. Back to bed.


01:08:40.913 --> 01:08:43.916
- Is the monster going to kill us?
- No.


01:08:44.416 --> 01:08:45.667
No way.


01:08:45.834 --> 01:08:48.253
I ain't gonna let it get anywhere near you.


01:08:48.337 --> 01:08:50.172
But I'm a Hatfield.


01:08:51.673 --> 01:08:55.385
Come on, you ought to be sleeping.


01:08:56.220 --> 01:08:59.014
I'm going to kill you all.
I'm going to kill you all.


01:09:22.579 --> 01:09:23.956
Finish it.


01:09:28.252 --> 01:09:29.795
Kill them all.


01:09:33.215 --> 01:09:34.716
Kill them all.


01:09:38.387 --> 01:09:41.557
...good-for-nothing
and you always have been.


01:09:41.640 --> 01:09:44.393
- Shut up, you idiot.
- Yes, you are. Yes, you are.


01:09:44.434 --> 01:09:48.438
- Your family's past it.
- You know nothing, none of your family.


01:09:49.231 --> 01:09:52.401
This ain't even our problem.
All we gotta do is walk away.


01:09:52.484 --> 01:09:55.404
Let that thing kill them Hatfields.
What do we care?


01:09:55.445 --> 01:09:59.408
Hey! We got little ones in this house,
you son of a bitch.


01:09:59.449 --> 01:10:01.577
You gonna leave them to die, too?


01:10:01.660 --> 01:10:06.999
There's only one way to deal with this,
but you McCoys ain't gonna like it.


01:10:07.082 --> 01:10:09.334
- I don't care what they like.
- Shut your mouth.


01:10:09.418 --> 01:10:11.420
Let's just hear the man.


01:10:11.461 --> 01:10:15.257
I know what I'm talking about here.
There ain't no other way.


01:10:15.299 --> 01:10:17.426
You gotta trust me on that.


01:10:17.509 --> 01:10:20.095
There's no stopping this thing.


01:10:20.470 --> 01:10:25.767
You can't kill it, you can't reason with it
and you can't outrun it.


01:10:25.851 --> 01:10:29.605
It'll get you soon enough,
and it'll rip you to pieces.


01:10:29.688 --> 01:10:31.982
All right. So what do we have to do?


01:10:32.107 --> 01:10:33.692
You know who called it?


01:10:33.775 --> 01:10:35.360
Ricky McCoy.


01:10:35.444 --> 01:10:36.570
Yeah.


01:10:37.362 --> 01:10:40.407
The way they say he was acting at the wake,
you gotta say it was him.


01:10:40.490 --> 01:10:43.535
It's how they act,
the ones that summon the thing.


01:10:44.494 --> 01:10:45.829
It kills,


01:10:46.663 --> 01:10:48.749
and they feel it somehow.


01:10:49.333 --> 01:10:50.626
See it.


01:10:50.834 --> 01:10:54.171
- How come you know so much about this?
- Just trust me, I do.


01:10:54.296 --> 01:10:57.341
You're saying
there's something we gotta do?


01:10:59.134 --> 01:11:01.303
First thing you gotta do
is find Ricky McCoy.


01:11:01.386 --> 01:11:03.889
And once we find him? Then what?


01:11:03.972 --> 01:11:06.225
- Then you gotta kill him.
- No. No way.


01:11:06.308 --> 01:11:08.560
We're not going to kill our brother.


01:11:14.316 --> 01:11:17.069
- Does that mean the monster's coming?
- No.


01:11:17.236 --> 01:11:22.157
Just a storm. Normal, harmless storm.
Nothing to be scared of.


01:11:22.658 --> 01:11:26.995
Then how come there's thunder
and lightning and no rain?


01:11:29.164 --> 01:11:31.291
This ain't no normal storm.


01:11:32.209 --> 01:11:33.669
It's coming.


01:11:34.920 --> 01:11:37.256
Everybody's here in the house.


01:11:40.843 --> 01:11:42.719
We're well protected.


01:11:44.221 --> 01:11:46.765
They're just figuring a way
to sort things out.


01:11:46.849 --> 01:11:48.433
Can they do it?


01:11:49.935 --> 01:11:51.478
Sure they can.


01:12:06.577 --> 01:12:09.037
It's Ricky or all of us.


01:12:09.121 --> 01:12:12.875
- Yeah, he brought this on himself.
- Look. Ricky done wrong.


01:12:13.417 --> 01:12:16.920
- But we ain't going to kill our own brother.
- Then we'll do it.


01:12:17.045 --> 01:12:19.756
We're all gonna have to work together.


01:12:20.048 --> 01:12:21.425
First you gotta find him.


01:12:21.550 --> 01:12:25.012
You're expecting McCoys
to help hunt down one of our own?


01:12:25.095 --> 01:12:27.556
We got children in this house.


01:12:27.598 --> 01:12:31.435
You're gonna stand by
and let this thing kill them


01:12:31.560 --> 01:12:33.562
just to save your brother?


01:12:33.645 --> 01:12:35.397
Blood is blood.


01:12:35.439 --> 01:12:39.902
We didn't ask for this,
and now we're gonna protect our family.


01:12:39.943 --> 01:12:43.280
- Like we're trying to do right now.
- We didn't start this.


01:12:43.405 --> 01:12:46.992
Your boys killed our Sara.
Then, yeah, you did.


01:12:47.075 --> 01:12:48.660
Hey, hey, hey, hey!


01:12:48.744 --> 01:12:50.120
Hold it! Hey, hey!


01:12:50.245 --> 01:12:52.247
While you're wasting time
fighting each other,


01:12:52.331 --> 01:12:54.750
that thing is still out there.


01:12:56.084 --> 01:13:01.757
Long as Ricky McCoy's still alive,
there's no getting away from it.


01:13:01.798 --> 01:13:06.428
It'll find you, it'll kill you
and it'll move onto the next.


01:13:06.512 --> 01:13:10.557
It'll kill the men. It'll kill the women.
It makes no difference to it.


01:13:10.641 --> 01:13:12.434
It'll even kill the children.


01:13:16.939 --> 01:13:19.650
It will kill all those who are marked.


01:13:20.484 --> 01:13:23.570
It'll also kill anybody
who tries to get in its way.


01:13:23.654 --> 01:13:26.198
We're not talking about an animal.


01:13:26.615 --> 01:13:29.284
We're not talking about a man.


01:13:30.202 --> 01:13:32.829
This is a thing straight from hell,


01:13:33.121 --> 01:13:35.791
and it's here to kill a whole family


01:13:35.958 --> 01:13:38.627
and anybody else who gets in its way.


01:13:39.461 --> 01:13:42.297
This land's gonna be soaking in blood


01:13:42.506 --> 01:13:46.552
unless you find and kill Ricky McCoy.


01:13:46.635 --> 01:13:47.719
No!


01:13:48.470 --> 01:13:50.722
There's gotta be another way.


01:13:50.848 --> 01:13:53.892
I'm sorry, Jodie. There ain't no other way.


01:13:55.519 --> 01:13:57.396
But he's the man I love.


01:13:57.479 --> 01:13:59.731
We couldn't tell any of you


01:14:00.232 --> 01:14:05.070
'cause of this stupid feud
and all the bad feeling.


01:14:06.029 --> 01:14:10.909
We always had to sneak around
like we were doing something wrong.


01:14:11.660 --> 01:14:16.623
But we weren't. I love him and he loves me.


01:14:17.666 --> 01:14:19.668
And you can't kill him.


01:14:21.003 --> 01:14:22.379
Please.


01:14:22.921 --> 01:14:24.923
We'll find another way.


01:14:25.883 --> 01:14:27.968
There ain't no other way.


01:14:29.178 --> 01:14:32.556
Now, how come you know
so much about this?


01:14:36.268 --> 01:14:38.729
Five years ago,
my brother and I were driving around


01:14:38.854 --> 01:14:43.192
drunk as skunks one night,
and we hit a woman.


01:14:43.275 --> 01:14:45.527
We got scared and drove off.


01:14:46.361 --> 01:14:51.575
She died in a ditch beside the road,
probably hours later.


01:14:51.700 --> 01:14:53.911
I mean, we could've helped.


01:14:54.912 --> 01:14:58.916
We should've helped, but we were too afraid
of what our father was gonna do.


01:14:59.041 --> 01:15:01.919
A young man named Andy Mills


01:15:02.044 --> 01:15:05.756
found himself
putting his young wife into the ground.


01:15:05.964 --> 01:15:09.009
He knows we'd done it,
but he couldn't prove it,


01:15:09.092 --> 01:15:13.722
not when our father was the sheriff
and he was keeping things quiet.


01:15:15.599 --> 01:15:18.060
So Andy went off into the woods


01:15:18.477 --> 01:15:21.647
and he did what Ed Harley had done
before him.


01:15:21.730 --> 01:15:24.274
Called on this thing, Pumpkinhead.


01:15:26.610 --> 01:15:30.656
And I saw it kill my brother.


01:15:31.990 --> 01:15:36.537
And I went to Andy
and I begged him to call it off.


01:15:39.248 --> 01:15:43.168
But he couldn't, even if he wanted to.


01:15:44.086 --> 01:15:48.465
That thing damn near killed me, too.


01:15:51.093 --> 01:15:53.345
How'd you get away from that?


01:15:54.972 --> 01:16:00.018
Well, I figured I was gonna die anyway.


01:16:01.436 --> 01:16:03.814
I might as well take Andy with me.


01:16:04.022 --> 01:16:05.774
And I killed him.


01:16:05.941 --> 01:16:08.902
When he died, that thing was gone, too.


01:16:09.778 --> 01:16:11.363
And I learnt its secret that night,


01:16:11.446 --> 01:16:13.949
and it wasn't something
I was ever gonna forget.


01:16:14.032 --> 01:16:18.203
And that's how I know
what you all gotta do now.


01:16:19.288 --> 01:16:20.497
Please.


01:16:21.832 --> 01:16:23.709
Please don't do this.


01:16:25.335 --> 01:16:26.628
Sheriff.


01:16:40.726 --> 01:16:42.060
What is it?


01:16:42.561 --> 01:16:45.230
I see it. It's coming.


01:16:50.819 --> 01:16:52.529
- Do you hear something?
- What's going on?


01:16:52.654 --> 01:16:53.822
- I don't know.
- What's happened?


01:16:53.906 --> 01:16:55.157
I don't know.


01:16:59.369 --> 01:17:00.537
No!


01:17:00.829 --> 01:17:02.206
- No, Brett!
- Pull!


01:17:03.999 --> 01:17:07.336
Oh, my God! No!


01:17:13.550 --> 01:17:14.593
No!


01:17:23.727 --> 01:17:26.772
It ain't getting in here, boys. Come on.


01:17:32.528 --> 01:17:34.029
Finish it.


01:17:53.298 --> 01:17:55.259
- Come on, come on, pass them out.
- There we go.


01:17:55.384 --> 01:17:56.635
Tristan.


01:17:56.760 --> 01:17:58.345
Little Joe.


01:17:58.595 --> 01:18:00.055
Emmett.


01:18:00.097 --> 01:18:01.306
Mikey.


01:18:02.391 --> 01:18:05.310
Come on, boys. Get up there. Come on.


01:18:08.605 --> 01:18:10.899
- Does anybody see it?
- No.


01:18:10.983 --> 01:18:12.568
Let's get out of here.


01:18:12.901 --> 01:18:15.153
This is the Hatfields' problem.


01:18:15.237 --> 01:18:17.573
There ain't nothing we can't do
about that thing.


01:18:17.614 --> 01:18:19.950
- You saw it. You all saw it.
- Shut up.


01:18:20.409 --> 01:18:23.120
We stay and fight, then we all die, too.


01:18:23.245 --> 01:18:24.913
You heard what the Sheriff said.


01:18:24.997 --> 01:18:29.459
Everybody trying to protect
the ones it wants gets killed, too.


01:18:29.585 --> 01:18:31.628
You ain't gonna leave us.


01:18:31.753 --> 01:18:33.922
Come on.
We didn't bring this thing on ourselves.


01:18:34.006 --> 01:18:36.258
Look, there ain't nothing we can do,


01:18:36.341 --> 01:18:38.302
so what's the point of us staying
and dying, too?


01:18:38.427 --> 01:18:41.805
Would you shut up? I can't believe
I'm hearing this from one of my own boys.


01:18:41.930 --> 01:18:45.601
It's one of us that did this.
Ricky brought this death down here.


01:18:45.767 --> 01:18:49.605
Are we supposed to turn tail and run?
How are we supposed to live with that?


01:18:50.272 --> 01:18:54.109
It weren't the Hatfields that called it.
It's one of ours.


01:18:54.193 --> 01:18:58.322
We stay and fight
and we try to put right what Ricky's done.


01:19:03.619 --> 01:19:05.746
Now, let's kill this thing


01:19:05.996 --> 01:19:09.166
and send it back to hell, where it belongs.


01:19:10.292 --> 01:19:13.212
Remember what I told you.
Only you can stop it.


01:19:14.004 --> 01:19:16.131
- You can save his soul.
- How?


01:19:16.215 --> 01:19:19.176
You have to do the hardest thing there is.


01:19:23.639 --> 01:19:25.974
It's climbing the walls.


01:19:27.226 --> 01:19:29.144
It's on the roof.


01:20:14.273 --> 01:20:16.024
Get away from her!


01:20:27.578 --> 01:20:29.037
Tristan!


01:21:32.684 --> 01:21:33.810
Hey!


01:21:58.544 --> 01:22:01.380
Are you hurt? Are you hurt?


01:22:07.135 --> 01:22:08.303
Ricky.


01:22:46.008 --> 01:22:47.759
It's time, Dallas.


01:22:49.761 --> 01:22:52.181
I told you this time would come.


01:22:52.556 --> 01:22:53.974
I know.


01:22:54.224 --> 01:22:56.935
You have to go out there and face it.


01:22:57.311 --> 01:22:58.645
It's gonna kill me.


01:22:58.729 --> 01:23:01.940
I told you five years ago
there'd be no place to hide.


01:23:02.024 --> 01:23:05.235
Now, you and it
have got some unfinished business.


01:23:05.319 --> 01:23:07.154
You gotta finish it.


01:23:07.362 --> 01:23:11.617
You face it
and you can make some wrongs right.


01:23:13.368 --> 01:23:16.246
I am trying to save you from my fate,


01:23:16.455 --> 01:23:19.708
trapped between for all time.


01:23:20.417 --> 01:23:22.669
I can't even see my son.


01:23:23.337 --> 01:23:24.630
But you...


01:23:26.256 --> 01:23:28.258
You can save your soul.


01:23:36.058 --> 01:23:37.809
Don't do this!


01:23:38.018 --> 01:23:40.771
I ain't gonna sit by and let it kill my family.


01:23:40.854 --> 01:23:42.231
My son started this.


01:23:42.314 --> 01:23:45.609
This mess started
before your son was even born.


01:23:46.068 --> 01:23:47.611
- Stay back.
- What are you doing?


01:23:47.694 --> 01:23:52.157
Had five more years than I was supposed to,
but now it's my time.


01:24:06.421 --> 01:24:10.843
Ricky. Ricky, you have to stop it. Ricky.


01:24:10.926 --> 01:24:13.554
I did what I did
so that we could be together.


01:24:13.637 --> 01:24:18.433
Tell it to stop. Please, Ricky. Make it stop!


01:24:18.517 --> 01:24:20.435
- Ricky. Ricky.
- I can't.


01:24:20.519 --> 01:24:22.938
- Ricky, please. Ricky.
- I can't.


01:24:23.021 --> 01:24:26.149
Ricky. Ricky, please.


01:24:35.742 --> 01:24:40.873
I killed two people in my life.
I see their faces every time I go to sleep.


01:24:40.956 --> 01:24:43.083
Second one was 'cause of you.


01:24:43.333 --> 01:24:46.461
That's right. You remember me.


01:24:46.962 --> 01:24:48.755
I beat you before.


01:24:49.298 --> 01:24:52.885
It cost me. This one's for my brother,
you son of a bitch.


01:25:11.320 --> 01:25:14.114
Ricky, listen to me.


01:25:14.531 --> 01:25:16.950
Ricky, you have to stop it.


01:25:17.492 --> 01:25:20.829
- Listen to what it's doing, Ricky.
- Just stay out of its way.


01:25:20.913 --> 01:25:22.122
Ricky.


01:25:27.211 --> 01:25:28.587
- Sheriff!
- Jodie.


01:25:30.380 --> 01:25:35.219
I don't want it to hurt you,
but if you try and stop it, it will kill you, too.


01:25:39.181 --> 01:25:41.642
Smile, you son of a bitch.


01:26:00.869 --> 01:26:02.829
Dolly, run!


01:26:23.100 --> 01:26:25.060
You're gonna help my sister.


01:26:25.143 --> 01:26:30.065
They killed Sara. They started it.
What's done can't be undone.


01:26:30.148 --> 01:26:34.945
If you really love me, Ricky McCoy,
then you'll help me now!


01:26:38.115 --> 01:26:39.783
You bastard!


01:27:20.449 --> 01:27:21.700
No!


01:27:32.544 --> 01:27:37.049
Put her down! Not her. Put her down!


01:27:42.513 --> 01:27:45.474
Ricky, don't let it hurt her!


01:27:46.058 --> 01:27:48.143
Ricky!


01:27:49.603 --> 01:27:52.981
Oh, my God. What have I done?


01:27:55.150 --> 01:27:58.654
No. This wasn't the deal.
She's just a little girl.


01:27:58.737 --> 01:28:00.322
This isn't what I asked for.


01:28:00.405 --> 01:28:03.659
You were supposed to make it
so me and Jodie could be together.


01:28:03.742 --> 01:28:06.161
This isn't what I wanted!


01:28:17.506 --> 01:28:19.758
- Kill me.
- No.


01:28:20.384 --> 01:28:22.845
- No.
- It's the only way.


01:28:23.011 --> 01:28:25.013
I know you can do it.


01:28:30.310 --> 01:28:34.273
I know you can do it. It's the only way.
You got no choice.


01:28:39.653 --> 01:28:43.115
- I can't shoot you, Ricky.
- Please, Jodie.


01:28:43.198 --> 01:28:45.909
I got enough blood on my hands.


01:28:49.371 --> 01:28:51.373
No, I can't do it!


01:28:51.748 --> 01:28:53.208
I love you.


01:28:56.420 --> 01:28:58.005
I love you.


01:29:35.792 --> 01:29:37.377
Do it, Jodie!


01:29:41.965 --> 01:29:43.217
No!


01:30:32.516 --> 01:30:33.934
Is it gone?


01:30:37.062 --> 01:30:38.313
It's over.


01:30:40.148 --> 01:30:44.403
There ain't nothing harder
than letting go of someone you love.


01:30:48.407 --> 01:30:50.200
We are what we do.


01:30:51.785 --> 01:30:53.662
You done good, Jodie.


01:30:55.038 --> 01:30:56.582
You done good.

